  message: "Tier 2 verification: all three named instance items have shipped — WI-gupah (Jackson/JavaBean, 7614 candidates), WI-nutav (Airflow framework-dispatch, 4511 candidates), WI-lisov (Kafka Streams topology, 2386 candidates) — combined 14,511 candidates worth of within-language framework-dispatch FP-reduction. The roadmap-prioritization principle was applied with positive results for one cycle. Cross-language items the description compared against (WI-tinip Elm→Go umbrella, WI-ropoz gRPC↔TS) remain in flight or open, consistent with the rank-by-volume principle. Recommend human flip to status=satisfied with this evidence; alternatively keep at needs_human_review if the human wants to see another cycle of prioritization before declaring the principle held."  # d355
